{"case_id":"T8001","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["input_semantics","API_protocol","state_coverage"],"confidence":99,"affected_functions":["archive_read_support_format_7zip","archive_read_format_7zip_bid","archive_read_format_7zip_read_header","slurp_central_directory","read_Header","read_StreamsInfo","read_PackInfo","read_CodersInfo","read_Folder","read_SubStreamsInfo","init_decompression","archive_read_format_7zip_read_data","archive_read_format_7zip_read_data_skip","skip_stream"],"reason":"H0 registers the new 7Zip reader indirectly through archive_read_support_format_all, but supplies no 7Zip seed. Its sparse byte mutations of unrelated ISO, CAB, LZH, tar, ZIP, RAR, and other images are not a meaningful way to satisfy the exact 7Zip signature and CRC-constrained header structure required to reach the new parser and decompression logic. H0 also always drains each entry with archive_read_data_block before requesting the next header, so it does not exercise the explicit unread-entry skip protocol implemented by archive_read_format_7zip_read_data_skip and skip_stream.","evidence":["S1 adds ARCHIVE_FORMAT_7ZIP and the public entry point archive_read_support_format_7zip.","archive_read_support_format_all now calls archive_read_support_format_7zip, so H0 can register the reader but still needs qualifying input to select it.","archive_read_format_7zip_bid requires memcmp(p, \"7z\\xBC\\xAF\\x27\\x1C\", 6) == 0.","slurp_central_directory additionally validates the signature CRC, next-header CRC, offsets, sizes, and structured property IDs before reaching read_Header and related parsing functions.","H0's files[] contains no .7z image; its listed seeds are ISO, CAB, LZH, bzip2/tar, gzip/tar, XZ/tar, ZIP, AR, CPIO/RPM, RAR, mtree, and tar images.","H0 changes fewer than about 1% of bytes in each existing image, making generation of a coherent 7Zip container from those non-7Zip seeds implausible.","H0 loops on archive_read_data_block until it stops for every header, whereas S1 introduces archive_read_format_7zip_read_data_skip and skip_stream for transitions where entry data is left unread."],"recommended_action":"Add valid 7Zip corpus seeds covering plain and encoded headers, multiple folders/substreams, empty entries, names/times/attributes, CRCs, and supported codec/filter combinations, then mutate the complete 7Zip image. Add a protocol variant that alternates full reads, partial reads, zero data reads followed by archive_read_next_header, and explicit archive_read_data_skip so skip_stream and subsequent folder/entry state transitions are exercised."}
